--TEST--
`Core\Program::implementing` refuses a type argument that is not an interface, a shape among them, and an interface one of whose classes has a constructor the enumeration could not call, each at the call that would have written the `new` (`rule:programs/implementing`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:attributes/core-program-implementing-i-every-class-implementing-an-interface
// `rule:programs/implementing`: the type argument is what gives the enumerated instances a
// static type and the enumeration writes `new C()` for each of them, so an
// argument that is not an interface and a class the enumeration could not
// construct are both refused where the call is written. The accepted call is
// first, so an enumeration that stopped answering a well-formed one fails here
// rather than as a missing refusal.
interface Check {
    public function name(): string;
}

class Fine implements Check {
    public function name(): string { return "fine"; }
}

class Plain {
    public function name(): string { return "plain"; }
}

interface Needful {
    public function label(): string;
}

// What a class needs arrives through the interface's own methods, because the
// enumeration has nothing to pass to a constructor.
class Needy implements Needful {
    public string $label;
    public function constructor(string $label) { $this->label = $label; }
    public function label(): string { return $this->label; }
}

echo Core\Arr::count(Core\Program::implementing<Check>()), "\n";

// A class describes an implementation rather than an interface to enumerate.
echo Core\Arr::count(Core\Program::implementing<Plain>()), "\n";

// A shape describes data rather than methods, so nothing could be called on
// the array it would answer.
echo Core\Arr::count(Core\Program::implementing<{name: string}>()), "\n";

// Every class the enumeration instantiates needs a constructor callable with
// no arguments.
echo Core\Arr::count(Core\Program::implementing<Needful>()), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0743]: `Core\Program::implementing` enumerates an interface, and `Plain` is not one
   --> case.nvs:36:22
%A
error[E0743]: `Core\Program::implementing` enumerates an interface, and `{name: string}` is not one
   --> case.nvs:40:22
%A
error[E0744]: `Needy` implements `Needful` and its constructor takes 1 required argument(s)
   --> case.nvs:44:22
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
